APPLICATION NOTE — read this first; it does not modify the terms below.

The SSAL text that follows is reproduced verbatim from the licence published at
github.com/aevov/cr8oskernel, and its clauses were drafted for the CR8OS Kernel.
Applied to this work, the operative provisions are Section 2 (Grant of Rights) and
Section 3 (Restrictions), which are generic to any work. Section 4 names the
"Blackwell-QP" anyonic protocol and "Merkle-Shard" storage logic, which are kernel
components and do not exist in this plugin; Section 4 is asserted here only for its
anti-decoupling intent, and no such claim is made about this work.

The licensed work is: Aevov Senton Field ("the Software"), the directory
aevov-senton-field/ and the files within it, together with the tuning table in
includes/class-senton-tuning.php. The rest of the Aevov-Web3 repository remains under
GNU Affero General Public License v3.0; see LICENSE and README.md at the repository root.

Anyone exercising the Section 2(a) audit right should know: the numeric tuning
constants in this plugin are deliberately encoded rather than written in place. They
are decodable, and decoding them is permitted — it is exactly the audit Section 2(a)
contemplates. The encoding is there to stop a drive-by copy-paste from getting a
tuned model, not to hide anything from an auditor. The restriction that actually
protects this work is Section 3, and it is a legal restriction, not a technical one.

One ambiguity is recorded rather than resolved silently. Section 3(b) forbids porting to
"any non-AevOS kernels, including but not limited to the Linux Kernel or BSD-based
systems"; that clause was drafted for a kernel. Read literally against a PHP plugin it
would forbid the ordinary operating system a mesh node runs on, which would empty
Section 2(b) of content. The intended scope here is the *software stack*: shipping or
re-targeting this field into a non-AevOS plugin set, host framework or product is the
prohibited act, in any operating system. If your intended use is not clearly permitted
by that reading, treat Section 3 as controlling and request written consent from the
Aevov Organization before doing it.
